          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The backing track now plays three chords of {{=key}}, a bar each. {{chord:I}} is the 1st chord of the key, built on {{1}}. {{chord:IV}} is the 4th chord, built on {{4}}, and {{chord:V}} is the 5th chord, built on {{5}}.\nPress Play below to start the backing track. On each chord, play a 3rd on beats 1 and 2 and a 6th on beats 3 and 4, both made of the chord's own notes.\nWhen the 3rd changes to a 6th, the chord under it stays: listen for the moment the pair gets wider.\n{{?key}}In another key the pairs sit on other frets, and each 3rd and 6th still shares its lower note on the G string."
